---
/* THESIS: Landing as a vertical rise through protocol courses; refuses gradient-card SaaS heroes.
   OWN-WORLD: Slate, copper, Source Serif display, rustdoc path kickers, hairline app rows.
   STORY: What Tangled is, why, the apps on it, then the spec.
   FIRST VIEWPORT: Monumental serif line, one paragraph, Read the spec / GitHub.
   FORM: Courses (dea6db17 #7), Comp B plates. */
import LandingLayout from "../layouts/LandingLayout.astro";
import { githubUrl, withBase } from "../data/nav";

const apps = [
  {
    id: "apps::reed",
    name: "Reed",
    href: `${githubUrl}/tree/main/apps/reed`,
    copy: "Public posts, profiles, follows, a home timeline. The social client on the data plane.",
  },
  {
    id: "apps::loomed",
    name: "Loomed",
    href: `${githubUrl}/tree/main/apps/loomed`,
    copy: "Sealed messages for circles. A radio set for the people you already trust — not a column of bubbles.",
  },
  {
    id: "apps::weft",
    name: "Weft",
    href: `${githubUrl}/tree/main/apps/weft`,
    copy: "A read-only explorer. Counts, topology, lookup. It does not write.",
  },
];
---

<LandingLayout>
  <section class="land-hero">
    <p class="land-kicker">tangled::protocol</p>
    <h1>A content network you host.</h1>
    <p class="land-lead">
      Identity is a Solana Ed25519 public key. Content lives in a signed Merkle repository on a host
      you control — a <strong>knot</strong>. Authorization is object-capability. Confidentiality is
      encryption. Discovery and moderation are unprivileged overlays.
    </p>
    <div class="land-cta">
      <a class="btn-primary" href={withBase("/docs")}>Read the spec</a>
      <a class="btn-ghost" href={githubUrl} rel="noopener noreferrer">GitHub</a>
    </div>
    <p class="land-aside">This site is a specification, not a running network. There is no public graph to join.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="land-course" aria-labelledby="why">
    <p class="land-kicker">tangled::why</p>
    <h2 id="why">One data plane. The knot is not a priest.</h2>
    <p>
      Neighboring protocols split the public tree from private data, or ask you to treat the host as
      an authority. Tangled keeps public, capability-gated, and sealed records in one repository and
      one sync protocol. Visibility is a field. A knot is a convenient place to keep bytes — it is
      not an authority over identity, history, or meaning. Any replica can be verified from the
      signatures and the Merkle root.
    </p>
    <p>
      Followers pull. Authors do not POST into N inboxes. Relays are not the source of truth. The
      source of truth is a signed commit. One process and a local database is enough to exist.
      Optional <strong>looms</strong> index public heads. Gateways bind other networks with
      provenance; they do not define the data model.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="land-course" aria-labelledby="knot">
    <p class="land-kicker">tangled::knot</p>
    <h2 id="knot">How the pieces sit.</h2>
    <div class="arch" role="list">
      <div class="arch-row" role="listitem">
        <code>wallet</code>
        <span>Ed25519 sign. The identity is the key, rotatable in-repo.</span>
      </div>
      <div class="arch-row" role="listitem">
        <code>knot</code>
        <span>Merkle Search Tree and blobs. The host you control.</span>
      </div>
      <div class="arch-row" role="listitem">
        <code>sync</code>
        <span>Peers pull commits. Knots do not fan out inbox POSTs.</span>
      </div>
      <div class="arch-row" role="listitem">
        <code>loom</code>
        <span>Optional public index. Unprivileged. Not required to exist.</span>
      </div>
      <div class="arch-row" role="listitem">
        <code>gateway</code>
        <span>ActivityPub, Nostr, AT Protocol bind in with provenance.</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="land-course" aria-labelledby="apps">
    <p class="land-kicker">tangled::apps</p>
    <h2 id="apps">Applications on the substrate.</h2>
    <p>
      Microblogs, private groups, and explorers are clients of one data plane. The protocol does not
      privilege a social-network shape. These three live in this repository. They are not a hosted
      service.
    </p>
    <ul class="land-apps">
      {
        apps.map((app) => (
          <li>
            <a href={app.href} rel="noopener noreferrer">
              <code>{app.id}</code>
              <span>
                <strong>{app.name}</strong>
                {app.copy}
              </span>
            </a>
          </li>
        ))
      }
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="land-course land-close" aria-labelledby="spec">
    <p class="land-kicker">tangled::spec</p>
    <h2 id="spec">The documents are the product.</h2>
    <p>
      Version 1 is implementable: chapters, Concise Data Definition Language (CDDL), OpenAPI, and
      test vectors. Start at the overview, jump the <a href={withBase("/reference/http")}>HTTP reference</a>,
      or open the <a href={withBase("/playground")}>synthetic playground</a>.
    </p>
    <div class="land-cta">
      <a class="btn-primary" href={withBase("/docs")}>Enter the spec</a>
      <a class="btn-ghost" href={withBase("/reference/http")}>HTTP methods</a>
    </div>
    <p class="land-aside">
      Preview this site locally with <code>just docs</code>. Run a knot with the recipes in the
      repository — this page will not start one for you.
    </p>
  </section>
</LandingLayout>
